    "Cached architecture geometry/materials retained renderer dispose registrations. Cleanup now releases GPU registrations while retaining bounded CPU buffers and refreshes overlapping live renderers.",
    "After cleanup, Castle DOM node/listener counts remain exactly constant from switch 10 through 40; the late heap slope drops 95.1 percent.",
    "The Graph-only control has residual late heap growth too. These measurements do not establish zero long-term JS growth, native-memory bounds, or real-GPU performance."
